AI-policy zones (Dr. Gaur): [G] green (I can help) · [A] amber (needs your prior approval) · [R] red (your intellectual contribution — I leave the guiding question).
01 · Title [G]
An advisory digital twin for energy-and-capacity optimization in mid-sized Peruvian data centers with limited telemetry: the INSUR pilot case.
02 · Abstract [R] — 1 paragraph, ~5 lines. Guide: problem → method (Design Science) → artifact → evaluation → contribution. 
03 · Introduction & Problem Statement [G/A] — must pass the "So what?" test.
Gap: mid-sized Peruvian DCs operate without full telemetry or digital twins; INSUR (SBS-supervised) as a bounded pilot. Opening figures with citation (Gartner 290 GW by 2030; Peru 14 DCs). Why care: energy cost and capacity risk are the top operational constraints for these sites, and no validated advisory-twin design principles exist for them.
04 · Literature Review [A] — needs prior approval.
Axes: digital twins (advisory vs. autonomous), Design Science (Hevner 2004; Peffers 2007; Gregor & Hevner 2013), FEDS evaluation (Venable 2016), PUE and energy proportionality.
05 · Research Questions & Objectives [R] — DSR ⇒ research questions, not hypotheses.
RQ: (refined in Session 2).
General objective: design and evaluate an advisory twin for energy and capacity.
Specific objectives (3, SMART — Doran 1981: Specific, Measurable, Assignable, Realistic, Time-related): ① build the artifact; ② validate it (model + decision utility); ③ abstract transferable design principles.
Note: Design Science defaults to research questions, not hypotheses
06 · Methodology [R] — paradigm already fixed (Design Science).
Peffers 6-step process · FEDS evaluation · interrupted time series (Bernal 2017) · metrics: PUE + energy proportionality · multi-site for transferability.
07 · Ethical Considerations [G] — a chapter, not a checkbox.
Align with CONCYTEC Código Nacional de Integridad Científica (Res. N° 028-2024-CONCYTEC-P) and Ley 32098 (fraud sanctions). Personal data: Ley 29733 + DS 016-2024-JUS. AI deployment: Ley 31814 + DS 115-2025-PCM. Include: consent (scope for secondary data), risks + mitigation, storage/access plan, conflict of interest, AI-use declaration.
08 · Expected Results [R]
Validated artifact + transferable design principles; measurable improvement in decisions (and PUE) vs. baseline.
09 · Timeline & Budget [G]
3 years; CEI (UNMSM Research Ethics Committee) approval first — plan 2–6 months; add a 25–30% buffer row. Budget: MVP + sensors/software (investment to justify).
